    questionText: "Suppose \\( H \\) has the asymptotic series \\( H(x)\\sim\\sum_{n\\ge 0}\\alpha_n x^{n} \\) as \\( x\\to 0^{+} \\), and that \\( H' \\) is continuous on \\( [0,\\infty) \\) and also possesses an asymptotic series \\( H'(x)\\sim\\sum_{n\\ge 0}\\beta_n x^{n} \\). Prove that \\( \\beta_n=(n+1)\\alpha_{n+1} \\).",
