    questionText: "It is given that \\( E_1(x)+\\ln x \\to -\\gamma \\) as \\( x\\to 0^{+} \\), where \\( \\gamma \\) is Euler's constant. By differentiating \\( E_1(x)+\\ln x \\) and integrating the resulting series, find the first two non-constant terms of the small-\\( x \\) expansion of \\( E_1(x) \\).",
