    questionText: "Let \\( s(x)=\\sin x \\). Show that integrating the bound \\( s(x)=O(1) \\) over \\( [0,x] \\) is consistent with \\( \\int_0^x \\sin t\\,dt = O(1) \\), but that differentiating the (bounded) primitive does NOT lower the order. State, in one line, the general moral about which operation is safe.",
