    questionText: "Given \\( \\displaystyle G(x)=\\int_0^{\\infty}\\frac{e^{-t}}{(1+xt)^{2}}\\,dt \\sim \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}(-1)^n (n+1)!\\,x^{n} \\) as \\( x\\to 0^{+} \\), integrate the series term by term to find the asymptotic series of \\( \\displaystyle \\Phi(x)=\\int_0^x G(s)\\,ds \\). Identify the closed form of \\( \\Phi \\).",
