    questionText: "Suppose \\( f(x)=o(e^{x}) \\) as \\( x\\to\\infty \\) with \\( f \\) continuous. By integrating, find the sharpest order bound of the form \\( o(g(x)) \\) for \\( \\displaystyle\\int_0^x f(t)\\,dt \\), and explain why the naive answer \\( o(x e^{x}) \\) is not the sharpest here.",
