    questionText: "Starting from \\( E_1(x)\\sim e^{-x}\\sum_{n\\ge0}(-1)^n n!\\,x^{-n-1} \\) as \\( x\\to\\infty \\), confirm by differentiating term by term that the resulting series is consistent with the exact relation \\( E_1'(x)=-e^{-x}/x \\). State to what extent term-by-term differentiation is justified.",
