    questionText: "Define \\( \\displaystyle S(x)=\\int_0^x \\frac{\\sin t}{t}\\,dt \\) (so \\( S\\to\\pi/2 \\) as \\( x\\to\\infty \\)). Using integration by parts on \\( \\int_x^{\\infty}\\frac{\\sin t}{t}\\,dt \\), find the first two terms of the large-\\( x \\) expansion of \\( \\frac{\\pi}{2}-S(x) \\).",
