    questionText: "It is given that \\( \\displaystyle\\int_x^{\\infty}t^{-1}e^{-t}\\,dt = E_1(x) \\) has remainder bound \\( |\\text{Err}_N|\\le N!\\,e^{-x}x^{-N-1} \\). Using optimal truncation \\( N+1=\\lfloor x\\rfloor \\) and Stirling's formula, show the optimal error is \\( O\\big(x^{1/2}e^{-2x}\\big) \\) and hence beyond all algebraic orders relative to \\( e^{-x} \\).",
